add('Strict Clippy flags a manually implemented enum default','connection/assembler.rs:333',clippysrc,'not-defect',None,'Baseline strict Clippy reproduced derivable_impls on Rust 1.99.1. Deriving Default is a lint/style transformation, not a behavior defect.','skill-requested-hygiene')
add('Strict Clippy flags manual Option filtering','connection/packet_crypto.rs:91',clippysrc,'not-defect',None,'Baseline strict Clippy reproduced manual_filter on Rust 1.99.1. Replacing the equivalent expression is lint/style housekeeping.','skill-requested-hygiene')
add('u128 conversion allegedly truncates before validation','varint.rs:106',ids(107),'refuted',None,'The implementation uses checked x.try_into() before from_u64. Tests rejected (1u128<<64)+7, 1<<62, and u128::MAX; the largest valid value succeeded.')
add('Rejected 0-RTT retains discarded send-window charges','connection/streams/state.rs:244',ids(130,156,(204,209)),'ran','medium','A real resumption/rejection simulation filled a 13-byte send window. After handshake success, resending on the replacement stream returned Blocked. zero_rtt_rejected leaves unacked_data charged.')
add('Stopping a reset stream fails to advertise replacement stream credit','connection/streams/mod.rs:154',ids(131,159,(210,215)),'ran','medium','With one permitted incoming stream, an empty RESET followed by accept and stop left the peer unable to open its next stream after driving both endpoints. stop frees state without queue_max_stream_id.')
add('Zero idle timeout rejects immediate server acceptance','endpoint.rs:545',ids(133,158),'ran','medium','A server configured with Some(IdleTimeout(0)) rejected an immediately accepted valid Initial with TimedOut. The staleness check treats disabled timeout zero as an immediate deadline.')
add('BBR bandwidth maximum never expires lower samples','congestion/bbr/bw_estimation.rs:65',ids(138,164,(240,245)),'ran','medium','After measuring 1000000 bytes/s and then 28 rounds at 100000 bytes/s, the estimate remained 1000000. Lower samples never reach the ten-round maximum filter.')
add('MTU datagram pruning drops payloads equal to the limit','connection/datagrams.rs:149',ids(142),'ran','medium','drop_oversized(5) removed a queued five-byte payload and reduced outgoing_total to zero. The retain predicate uses < although the contract discards only larger payloads.')
add('Zero idle-timeout advertisement allegedly disables a finite peer timeout','connection/mod.rs:4067',ids(145),'refuted',None,'The helper explicitly preserves the nonzero timeout when the other value is zero/None. Tests with 0 and 5000 in both orders returned Some(5 seconds).')
add('Overlapping acknowledgments allegedly double-free send-buffer bytes','connection/send_buffer.rs:42',ids(146),'refuted',None,'ack clamps ranges to the tracked prefix and merges them through RangeSet. The reported 0..4, 8..12, 8..12, 2..6 sequence left exactly two unacked bytes (gh), which acknowledged normally.')
add('Connection credit exhaustion hides a stopped-stream write error','connection/streams/mod.rs:254',ids(155),'ran','medium','With 100 bytes of connection credit consumed across two streams, STOP_SENDING(42) made stopped() return Some(42), but another write returned Blocked instead of Stopped(42). The limit check precedes stream terminal-state handling.')
add('RESET then STOP returns receive credit twice','connection/streams/recv.rs:95',ids(160),'ran','medium','For 32 unread bytes in a 100-byte window, RESET raised local_max_data to 132; subsequent stop incorrectly raised it to 164. Recv::stop credits bytes already discarded by reset.')
add('Path MTU reset leaves an oversized datagram blocking the queue','connection/mod.rs:1399',ids(161),'ran','medium','After a path change reduced payload capacity from 1414 to 1162 and the new link MTU was 1200, driving the connection delivered no queued small datagram behind the old large one. The otherwise identical small-only control passed.')
add('Sparse CID rotation allegedly advances into an empty slot','cid_queue.rs:92',ids(173),'refuted',None,'iter yields each occupied slot\'s actual ring displacement, not its filtered ordinal. The 0,2,4 sequence rotated to IDs 2 and 4 with correct active sequence numbers and no panic.')
add('Switching to unordered reads allegedly exposes buffered duplicates','connection/assembler.rs:40',ids(175),'refuted',None,'ensure_ordering(false) calls defragment before building received ranges. The reported overlapping/duplicate 3..6 and 4..8 buffers, after reading 0..3, delivered offsets 3..7 exactly once.')
with open('/work/tmp/independent-report.jsonl','w') as f:
 for x in items: f.write(json.dumps(x)+'\n')
print('Union items:',len(items))
from collections import Counter
print('Statuses:',dict(Counter(x['status'] for x in items)))
print('Severities:',dict(Counter(x['severity'] for x in items)))
claimed=set().union(*(set(x['sources']) for x in items))
for p in passages.values():
 if p['id'] not in claimed and int(p['id'][1:]) < 119:
  print('Ungrouped early passage:',p['id'],p['text'][:100].replace('\n',' '))
